FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** José Valim holds most of `lib/`, but his last commit there was in 2015, so he is probably not reachable for review. Kaito Mori is the active owner to ask. `test/` is owned by mostly the same people, with a different spread.

**lib/** (1,248 lines in 17 files)

| Person | Lines | Share | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| José Valim (2 addresses) | 758 | 60.7% | last commit 2015-01-27, inactive |
| Kaito Mori | 220 | 17.6% | last commit 2026-10-10, active |
| Rafael Mendonça França (3 addresses) | 46 | 3.7% | last commit 2022-03-25, inactive |
| Carlos Antonio da Silva | 42 | 3.4% | last commit 2026-04-06, active |
| Vestimir Markov | 42 | 3.4% | last commit 2016-03-08, inactive |

- **Other authors:** the next rows are Jan De Poorter (2.5%) and Lucas Mazza (2.1%). 18 more authors hold the rest.
- **Who to ask:** the three people with the most lines in `lib/` are Valim, Mori and Mendonça França. Of those, only Mori is active. Among people active in the last year, Mori is followed by Silva (42 lines) and Gannon McGibbon (4 lines, 0.3%).
- **José Valim's two addresses:** `<email redacted>` has 476 lines (38.1%) and `<email redacted>` has 282 lines (22.6%). I counted them as one person because the names match. That is a guess from names and addresses. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`.
- **Bus factor in `lib/`:** this counts the fewest authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines.
  - Merged, Valim alone gives 1.
  - Unmerged, it is 2.
  - To reach 80% takes 4 authors.

**test/** (1,534 lines in 22 files)

| Person | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| José Valim (2 addresses) | 870 | 56.7% |
| Rafael Mendonça França (3 addresses) | 171 | 11.1% |
| Kaito Mori | 137 | 8.9% |
| Carlos Antonio da Silva | 103 | 6.7% |
| Lucas Mazza | 56 | 3.7% |

- **Other authors:** Jan De Poorter has 3.5% and Nando Vieira 2.2%. 8 more authors are not shown.
- **Is it the same group?** Mostly. Valim leads both, at 56.7% of `test/` and 60.7% of `lib/`.
- **Where it differs:** Mendonça França holds 11.1% of `test/` against 3.7% of `lib/`. Mori holds less of `test/` (8.9%) than of `lib/` (17.6%).
- **Bus factor in `test/`:** it is 1 when Valim's addresses are merged and 2 when they are not.

**What the numbers leave out**
- **Left out:** `Gemfile.lock` (174 lines) is excluded as a lockfile. The bots Weblate and github-actions[bot] are excluded, with 81 lines and 2 commits. Their lines are credited to nobody.
- **Reformat commit:** `46fafb7` ("Apply rubocop -A (Style/StringLiterals)") is listed in `.git-blame-ignore-revs`. It was ignored, so it did not take over anyone's lines.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** the tool checked for them and set aside none. In `lib/` it examined 90 commits holding surviving lines, and in the whole repo 222.
- **.mailmap:** it already merges `kmori <<email redacted>>` into Kaito Mori. That adds 20 lines to Mori's count.
- **Other possible duplicates:** the tool also suggested a merge for Rafael Mendonça França's 3 addresses and for Yuri S. These are guesses too.
- **Copy detection:** figures use `git blame -w -M -C`. Copy detection moved 89 lines to other authors across the repo. The largest effects are on Lucas Mazza (4.7% without it, 3.3% with it) and José Valim (48.0% without, 49.1% with). The tool listed no change over 2 points for the `lib/` authors named above.
- **Scope:** all 58 files were counted, not a sample. 3,467 of 3,548 lines were attributed.

Surviving lines show whose code is still there. They do not show who understands it, and they do not count review or design work.

